---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---
<Layout
  path="/privacy-policy/accessibility-check"
  title="Privacy Policy: Mithahara Accessibility Check"
  description="What the Mithahara Accessibility Check Shopify app reads from your store, what it keeps, and how it is deleted."
>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Privacy Policy: Mithahara Accessibility Check</h2>
      <p class="page-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        This page covers the Mithahara Accessibility Check app for Shopify. It scans your online
        store for accessibility problems and, on the paid plan, lets you write missing alt text
        for product images. Our <a href="/privacy-policy">general privacy policy</a> covers the
        rest of Mithahara. "We" means Mithahara.
      </p>

      <h3>What the app reads from your store</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your shop's domain, and the access token Shopify gives us when you install the app.</li>
        <li>
          The list of your pages, products and collections (titles and addresses), so the scan
          knows what to check.
        </li>
        <li>
          The public HTML of those pages, fetched the same way any visitor's browser would fetch
          them. It is checked for missing alt text, unlabeled form fields, skipped heading levels,
          a missing page language, and empty or vague links.
        </li>
        <li>
          Paid plan only: your product images, with their current alt text, so you can fill in
          the missing ones.
        </li>
        <li>Which plan you are on, from Shopify's billing system.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What we keep</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your shop domain, your plan, and the access token (stored encrypted).</li>
        <li>
          The results of each scan: the page address, the kind of problem, the fragment of page
          HTML the problem was found in, and whether it is still open. Those fragments come from
          your public pages, so they contain whatever text is published there.
        </li>
        <li>The alt text you type into the editor, and the time you saved it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Your customers' names, emails, addresses or orders, and any payment details. The app
          does not ask Shopify for customer, order or payment data.
        </li>
        <li>
          Anything from your store's visitors. The app adds no script, cookie or tracker to your
          storefront, and it changes nothing on your theme.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What the app changes in your store</h3>
      <p>
        Nothing, unless you are on the paid plan and press Save on an alt-text entry. That writes
        the text you typed to that one image through Shopify's API.
      </p>

      <h3>How we use it</h3>
      <p>
        Only to run your scans, show you the results, apply the alt text you approve, produce your
        report, and answer your support questions. We don't sell your data, use it for advertising,
        or use it to train AI models. The app does not send your pages to any AI service.
      </p>

      <h3>Who else handles it</h3>
      <p>
        Shopify (the platform you installed us from), and the cloud host that runs the app and its
        database. We share data with nobody else, except where the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h3>Uninstalling and deletion</h3>
      <p>
        When you uninstall, the access token stops working at once. Shopify then sends us a
        shop-erasure request, and we delete your shop's stored data, including scan results and
        alt-text history, when we receive it. If you want it gone sooner, or want to know what we
        hold about your shop, email us.
      </p>
      <p>
        Shopify's customer data requests (data request and erasure) reach us too. Because we hold
        no customer data, there is nothing to return or delete, and we confirm that to Shopify.
      </p>

      <h3>Your rights</h3>
      <p>
        If you are in the EU, UK or another region with data protection law, you can ask us for a
        copy of the data we hold about your shop, ask us to correct or delete it, and complain to
        your local data protection authority. The information we hold is limited to the list above.
      </p>

      <h3>Security</h3>
      <p>
        Data travels over HTTPS, and access tokens are encrypted at rest. No system is perfectly
        secure; if we learn of a breach affecting your shop we will tell you without undue delay.
      </p>

      <h3>Changes</h3>
      <p>
        If we change what the app collects, we will update this page and its date before the
        change goes live.
      </p>

      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <p>
        Questions or requests about this policy:{' '}
        <a href="mailto:support@mithahara.com">support@mithahara.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
